      "writtenOn": "2024-03-20T09:58:21Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "We don\u0027t need to zero the last byte at all, strlcpy inside bd_name_copy takes care of that now.\n\nWhen the BD_NAME is created using bd_name_from_char_pointer, we do zero remaining memory.\n\n\nSo this should create a closed circuit, where BD_NAME \"creation\" and passing is always safe.\n\nBTW. in UTF8, you can have code point 0 in middle of string and it\u0027s valid. \n\n\nMy next step would be to turn BD_NAME into a POD class, and have either copy constructor, or constructor that takes string as argument, and no default constructor (if possible), to have the safety of passing it verified during compilation.",
      "parentUuid": "bdc106c9_497a2078",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1997,
